*** Fork notes:

This is yet another fork of Dominic Radermacher's Ptouch-Print. Dominic has chosen keeps all
development centralized on their servers which is their choice. Do not contact Dominic about this
fork. This fork exists for me to keep track of some small tweaks as needed for my environment and
use cases.

Building and installing:
```sh
# install deps (may be incomplete)
sudo apt-get install libgd-dev libusb-1.0-0-dev
# build and install
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
make -j
sudo make install
```

Updating the fork:
```sh
git remote add upstream https://git.familie-radermacher.ch/linux/ptouch-print.git/
git fetch upstream
# now compare `upstream/master` against `fairx-main` and bring up to date
```

More info can be found at [upstream's
website](https://dominic.familie-radermacher.ch/projekte/ptouch-print/)

*** Original README below:

About:

ptouch-print is a command line tool to print labels on Brother P-Touch
printers on Linux.

There is no need to install the printer via CUPS, the printer is accessed
directly via libusb.

The tool was written for and tested with the PT-2430PC, but meanwhile is also
used with others (see "ptouch-print --list-supported")
Maybe others work too (please report USB VID and PID so I can include support
for further models, too).

Further info can be found at:
https://dominic.familie-radermacher.ch/projekte/ptouch-print/

Compile instructions:

./build.sh

Note:

Dear visitor, currently I have absolutely no time for improvements on this
project (my free time currently is about one or two hours PER MONTH).
Therefore, I can not look at suggestions about improvements.
